        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 81-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited marked dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation consistent with COPD without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Continuous pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout. Clinical condition improved satisfactorily, and the patient was discharged in stable condition. I recommend continuation of his inhaled bronchodilator regimen and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
